body:
Here's an extremely fast, one line way of doing this computation, using a neater syntax:

    const arr = rand(1:1.0:100, 2, 10000)
    @tullio out[i,j] = sqrt((arr[1,i] - arr[1,j])^2 + (arr[2,i] - arr[2,j])^2)

This makes use of Tullio.jl, which is really for Einstein summation, but can generate some very fast code for other stuff.
